SUMMARY: Doors Open Brampton Road Trip — Heritage\, History & Hidden Gem
 s! $20
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# Doors
  Open Brampton Road Trip — Heritage\, History & Hidden Gems!\n\n**Saturd
 ay\, October 3\, 2026**\n\nReady to explore Brampton from a whole new pers
 pective? Join us for a Saturday road trip to[ ](https://www.doorsopenontar
 io.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)**[Doors Open Brampton](https://www.doorsop
 enontario.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)**[\, ](https://www.doorsopenontario
 .on.ca/pages/events/brampton)where historic buildings\, museums\, heritage
  sites and other interesting spaces open their doors to the public.\n\n###
  🚗 The Road Trip\n\nWe'll meet **outside Christie Station at 8:30 AM** 
 and travel together in a **Kia Soul equipped with SiriusXM radio**. 🎶\n
 We'll head to Brampton for a day of exploring\, with a focus on the downto
 wn area so we can walk between several locations.\n\n### 💵 COST: $20\n\
 nThere is a **$20 charge for this event**.\nYour $20 covers:\n\n* 🚗 Rou
 nd-trip transportation from Toronto to Brampton\n* ⛽ Fuel\n* 🔧 Other 
 car operating expenses\n\n**Doors Open Brampton itself is free** — the $
 20 is strictly to cover the cost of transportation and operating the vehic
 le.\n\n### ⚠️ VERY LIMITED SPOTS!\n\nThis is a **very limited-capacity
  road trip**\, so if you're interested\, **sign up quickly!**\nTo lock in 
 your spot\, please send a **$20 e-transfer to:**\nnicolasbello@yahoo.com\n
 \n**Your spot is not confirmed until the $20 e-transfer has been received.
 **\n\n### 🏛️ [Exploring Brampton](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/
 pages/events/brampton)\n\nWe'll focus on the downtown area and visit as ma
 ny interesting Doors Open locations as we can within our limited time.\nPo
 ssible stops include:\n**📍 Brampton Downtown Heritage Walk**\nExplore B
 rampton's history\, architecture and stories from the city's past.\n**📍
  Alderlea**\nA beautifully preserved **1867 Italianate villa** overlooking
  Gage Park.\n**📍 Peel Art Gallery\, Museum & Archives (PAMA)**\nExplore
  exhibitions\, museum spaces and special Doors Open programming.\n**📍 B
 rampton Library – Four Corners Branch**\nCheck out this downtown locatio
 n and its local-history resources.\nWe'll add other participating Doors Op
 en locations as time permits.\n\n### ⏰ IMPORTANT TIMING\n\n**8:30 AM** 
 — Meet outside Christie Station\n**8:30 AM** — Depart Toronto\n**10:00
  AM** — Doors Open Brampton begins\n**10:00 AM–3:00 PM** — Explore B
 rampton\n**3:00 PM SHARP** — Depart Brampton for Toronto\n\n⚠️ **The
  3 PM departure is firm!**\nNick has a **Nuit Blanche volunteer shift in T
 oronto**\, so we absolutely need to leave Brampton at **3:00 PM sharp**.\n
 That gives us roughly five hours to explore\, so we'll keep things moving 
 and make the most of our time.\n\n### 🎶 THE RIDE\n\nTravel in a **Kia S
 oul with SiriusXM radio**\, good conversation and hopefully some great fal
 l weather.\nThe ride there and back is part of the fun!\n\n### 👟 WHAT T
 O BRING\n\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Weather-appropriate clothing\n* 
 Water\n* Camera/phone\n* Money for lunch\, coffee or snacks\n* Your curios
 ity!\n\n**Rain or shine — we're going!**\n\n### 📌 MEETING POINT\n\n**
 Outside Christie Station**\n**8:30 AM SHARP**\nPlease arrive a few minutes
  early so we can leave on time.\n\n### 💰 RESERVE YOUR SPOT\n\n**$20 per
  person**\n📧 Send your **$20 e-transfer to** nicolasbello@yahoo.com to 
 lock in your spot.\n🚨 **VERY LIMITED SPOTS AVAILABLE — SIGN UP FAST I
 F YOU'RE INTERESTED!**\n\nCome explore Brampton's history\, architecture a
 nd hidden gems with us! 🏛️🚗
