SUMMARY:Fall Walk: From Cabbagetown to Cherry Street 🌿 🍺
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂 
 Fall Walk: From Rosedale to Cherry Street 🌿\n\n### A Fall Walk Through 
 Some of Toronto's Most Interesting Neighbourhoods\n\nLooking for a walk th
 at gives you a little bit of everything?\nWe'll start in **Rosedale**\, ma
 ke our way through **Cabbagetown and Regent Park**\, wander through the **
 Distillery District**\, stop at **Biidaasige Park**\, and finish with a we
 ll-earned meal at **Cherry Street Bar-B-Que**.\nAlong the way\, we'll see 
 some of the city's oldest neighbourhoods\, newer communities\, historic ar
 chitecture\, green spaces\, and some pretty great views.\nIt's a longer wa
 lk\, but the route is more about **exploring Toronto together** than tryin
 g to finish as quickly as possible.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **Wha
 tsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrK
 Anc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet outside **Ro
 sedale Station** and begin our walk through Rosedale Valley\, following th
 e tree-lined route toward Cabbagetown.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk thr
 ough Rosedale Valley 🌳\n* Explore the historic streets of Cabbagetown\n
 * Pass through Regent Park\n* Wander through the Distillery District\n* St
 op at Biidaasige Park\n* Take in the fall scenery and city views\n* Finish
  at **Cherry Street Bar-B-Que** 🍖\n\nThe walk includes a **long set of 
 stairs**\, so while this isn't a difficult hike\, you should be comfortabl
 e walking for several hours and keeping up with the group.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🏙️ A Little Toronto History Along the Way\n\nThis walk takes us throu
 gh several very different parts of Toronto.\nIn **Cabbagetown**\, we'll pa
 ss beautifully preserved Victorian homes and streets that reflect the neig
 hbourhood's long history\, including its Irish roots.\n\nWe'll then make o
 ur way through **Regent Park**\, one of Toronto's most historically signif
 icant communities\, where older social housing has been joined by new hous
 ing\, arts\, and community spaces.\nFrom there\, we'll head into the **Dis
 tillery District**\, with its cobblestone streets and historic red-brick b
 uildings.\n\nWe'll also stop at **Biidaasige Park**\, whose name means *
 “the sun is shining”* in Anishinaabemowin.\nIt's a lot of Toronto in o
 ne walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 The Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\nWe'll finish
  our walk at **The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**\, right on the Keating Ch
 annel.\n\nThere's a bit of history behind this stop. The pub struggled dur
 ing the massive Port Lands construction\, when road closures and the reloc
 ation of the Cherry Street bridge made the area difficult to reach. With t
 he Port Lands now transformed and **Biidaasige Park** open\, people are re
 discovering this part of the city — and the pub is getting a second chan
 ce.\n\nAfter exploring the new park and the transformed Port Lands\, we'll
  finish at one of the neighbourhood's old survivors: a casual waterfront p
 ub with a patio overlooking the Keating Channel.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weath
 er & Expectations\n\nThis is a **long urban walk**\, not a difficult hike\
 , but you should be comfortable being on your feet for several hours.\nThe
 re is a long set of stairs along the route.\nPlease wear comfortable walki
 ng shoes and dress appropriately for the weather.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup
  Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Rosedale Station\n🫎 **Loo
 k for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM sharp\nI will o
 nly wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **En
 d Point:** Cherry Street Bar-B-Que\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5
  cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis 
 fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events th
 roughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comf
 ortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧴 Sunscreen\n🧥 Weather-appropri
 ate clothing\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:
 \n\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto\n* Anyone who likes history and a
 rchitecture\n* People looking for a longer social walk\n* Anyone who wants
  to discover neighbourhoods they might not normally visit\n* People who en
 joy stopping for food at the end\n* Anyone who wants to spend a Sunday exp
 loring the city with other people\n\nThe destination isn't really the poin
 t.\n**It's the people you meet along the way.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP 
 ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your sched
 ule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or chang
 ed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organi
 zer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesa
 ndoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the walk.**\n**Stay for the friends
 hip.**\n**And maybe stay a little longer for lunch.** 🍺🌿
