SUMMARY:🍁 Fall Walk: Finch Recreational Trail & Park Adventure! 🌾
 🚶‍♂️ (16KM) 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍁 
 Fall Walk: Finch Recreational Trail & Park Adventure! 🌾\n\n### An Easy\
 , Flat Fall Walk Through Toronto's Green Spaces\n\nLooking for an easy way
  to enjoy the fall colours without tackling a difficult hike?\nJoin us for
  a relaxed walk from **Pioneer Village Station to Finch Station**\, travel
 ling through Black Creek Parkland and along the **Finch Recreational Trail
 **.\n\nThis is one of our members' favourite walks for a reason. The route
  is mostly flat and takes us through open fields\, wooded areas\, and quie
 t green spaces that feel surprisingly far removed from the city.\n\nWe'll 
 take our time\, enjoy the changing leaves\, stop for a break by **Dufferin
  Creek**\, and spend the day walking and getting to know each other.\n\n
 📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://ch
 at.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What 
 We'll Do\n\nWe'll start outside **Pioneer Village Station** and make our w
 ay through Black Creek Parkland before joining the Finch Recreational Trai
 l.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk through Black Creek Parkland 🌳\n* Fo
 llow the Finch Recreational Trail\n* Enjoy the fall colours and changing s
 cenery 🍂\n* Stop for a break near Dufferin Creek\n* Have some time for 
 conversation and photos\n* Continue along the trail toward Finch Station\n
 \nThis is a **long but easy\, mostly flat walk**. There are no major hills
  or difficult terrain\, but you'll want comfortable shoes and enough energ
 y for the full route.\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 Fall Is the Best Time to Do This W
 alk\n\nThere's something particularly nice about this trail in the fall. T
 he air is cooler\, the leaves are changing\, and the open stretches of the
  trail give you plenty of room to slow down and enjoy the season.\nIt's a 
 good walk if you want to get outside without feeling like you're climbing 
 a mountain.\nAnd as always\, **the activity is the container. The people y
 ou meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup 
 Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Pioneer Village Station\, at 
 the corner of Steeles Avenue West and Northwest Gate (East Side)\, in fron
 t of the York University sign.\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰
  **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM sharp\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early
  is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Finch Station\n\n***\
 n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **ma
 thewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us 
 to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What t
 o Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack or lig
 ht lunch\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?
 \n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who enjoys fall scenery\n* People 
 looking for an easy\, flat trail\n* Anyone who wants to get back into walk
 ing\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto's green spaces\n* Anyone looking
  for a relaxed social outing\n* People who want to meet new people while g
 etting some fresh air\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show
  up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things hap
 pen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye
  on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? 
 Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n
 \n**Come for the fall colours.**\n**Stay for the friendship.** 🍁💛
